# CXREF: Called by bespoke DepoXy ctags wrapper:
#   ~/.kit/sh/home-fries/bin/ctags-groom.sh
# - Which is called by bespoke ohmyrepos infuse:
#   ~/.depoxy/ambers/home/.projlns/infuse-projlns-core.sh
# - Which generates this tags file:
#   DEPOXY_PROJLNS_DEPOXY/tags
#   - E.g.:
#     ~/.projlns/depoxy-deeplinks/tags
#   - SIZED/2026-05-31: Today, author's tags file is 887M
#     (by Universal Ctags; or ~1.4G if by Exuberant Ctags).
# - Also, ~/.ctags.d/config.ctags wired on 'infuse' by:
#     infuse_symlinks_user_home_dotfiles() {
#       ~/.depoxy/ambers/home/infuse-user-home
#   - And ~/.ctags.d/private.ctags wired by DXC infuse:
#       ~/.depoxy/ambers/mrassets/client-infuse

# +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++ #

# VERFY: After editing this file, verify it.
#
# - Most commands will fail if this config is broken; just run version:
#
#     ctags-universal --version

# VRIFY: If you twiddle with --langmap, verify it, e.g.:
#
#   $ ctags-universal --list-maps | grep "^Sh"
#   Sh       client-* *.sh *.SH *.bsh *.bash *.ksh *.zsh *.ash

# +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++ #

# REFER: Here are some of the common verification errors you might encounter:
#
#   $ ctags-universal --version
#   ctags-universal: Language "css" already defined
#
#   $ ctags-universal --version
#   ctags-universal: Warning: Don't reuse the kind letter `f' in a language Ruby (old: "method", new: "function")
#
#   $ ctags-universal --version
#   ctags-universal: Non-alphanumeric char is used in kind name: 'static field' in "--regex-coffee" option

# +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++ #

# PREVY: To verify Exuberant Ctags:
# - E.g., you don't want this:
#
#   $ ctags --version
#   ctags: Warning: Ignoring non-option in /home/landonb/.ctags
#
#   Exuberant Ctags...
#   ...
#
# - Though that particular warning is caused by comments (incl.
#   these comments!) which Exub. does not support — and I'm
#   unsure if the config still works... or at least I couldn't
#   get a custom Sh file path to work from herein with Exub.:
#     --langmap=Sh:+(client-*)
#   But a similar CLI argument worked:
#     ctags ... --langmap='Sh:+(client-*)'
#   Though I didn't investigate further; I realized I needed
#   to update to Universal Ctags on Linux like I had done on
#   macOS DepoXy (years ago, I might add, didn't realize the
#   DepoXy Linux ctags feature was so outta date!).
#
# - AWARE: Note this file is checked on --version, and
#   Exuberant Ctags will complain about comments herein:
#
#   $ ctags --version
#   ctags: Warning: Ignoring non-option in /home/landonb/.ctags
#
#   Exuberant Ctags 5.9~svn20110310, Copyright (C) 1996-2009 Darren Hiebert
#     Addresses: <dhiebert@users.sourceforge.net>, http://ctags.sourceforge.net
#     Optional compiled features: +wildcards, +regex
#
#   - Which, in additional to smaller file size, faster runtime, and active
#     project maintenance, is a good reason to use Universal Ctags.
#
# - HSTRY/2026-05-31: This file originally found by the author
#   circa 2010-2015, but I don't know from where, just that it
#   was created while working on Cyclopath research project (as
#   indicated by all the ActionScript config).
#
#   - Note this config was originally ~/.ctags for Exuberant Ctags,
#     and has since been converted to ~/.ctags.d/config.ctags for
#     Universal Ctags — but we haven't updated eveything.
#
#     - We've commented anything Universal complained about.
#
#     - And I don't think you need to worry about overriding
#       Universal Ctags defaults that might be better than
#       anything in here, because Universal should squawk if
#       we try to redefine anything, e.g., a line line this:
#
#         --langdef=css
#
#       Will break ctags-universal until you fix this config:
#
#         $ ctags-universal --list-kinds=all
#         ctags-universal: Language "css" already defined

# INERT/FIXEM: There's disabled config below from Exub. Ctags, that
# doesn't work with Universal Ctags, which we have no plans to fix.
# - INERT: If we notice any issues using tags, then we might fix.
# - Some of the issue are because Univ. Ctags defines more langs.
#   than Exub. did.
#   - E.g., this old config that worked with Exub.:
#     --langdef=css
#     --langmap=css:.css
#     --regex-css=/^[ \t]*([^\t {][^{]{1,100})(\t| )*\{/\1/d,definition/
#   Will cause this failure with Univ.:
#     $ ctags-universal --list-kinds=all
#     ctags-universal: Language "css" already defined
#   And while we could try to disable --langdef and --langmap but
#   not --regex-css, I highly doubt we need to override or supplant
#   anything in Universal!
# - This file's main uses is to specify these options:
#     --exclude
#     --fields
#     --extras
#     --langmap
#   - Though note we could also pass these as CLI args (and some
#     we already do):
#       infuse_projects_links_core_generate_ctags
#         ~/.depoxy/ambers/home/.projlns/infuse-projlns-core.sh

# +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++ #

# REFER: Some of the Listing Options:
#
#   ctags-universal --list-features
#
#   ctags-universal --list-maps
#   ctags-universal --list-maps | grep ^Sh
#
#   ctags-universal --list-kinds=all | bat
#   ctags-universal --list-kinds-full | bat
#
#   ctags-universal --list-regex-flags
#
# - REFER: How to use a different config, at least according to GAIO, e.g.:
#
#     ctags-universal --options=NONE --options=~/.ctags.d/config.ctags --list-maps
#
# - [All of the] Listing Options:
#     ctags-universal --list-aliases[=(<language>|all)]
#     ctags-universal --list-excludes
#     ctags-universal --list-extras[=(<language>|NONE|all)]
#     ctags-universal --list-features
#     ctags-universal --list-fields[=(<language>|NONE|all)]
#     ctags-universal --list-kinds[=(<language>|all)]
#     ctags-universal --list-kinds-full[=(<language>|all)]
#     ctags-universal --list-languages
#     ctags-universal --list-map-extensions[=(<language>|all)]
#     ctags-universal --list-map-patterns[=(<language>|all)]
#     ctags-universal --list-map-rexprs[=(<language>|all)]
#     ctags-universal --list-maps[=(<language>|all)]
#     ctags-universal --list-mline-regex-flags
#     ctags-universal --list-output-formats
#     ctags-universal --list-params[=(<language>|all)]
#     ctags-universal --list-pseudo-tags
#     ctags-universal --list-regex-flags
#     ctags-universal --list-roles[=(<language>|all)[.(<kind-specs>|*)]]
#     ctags-universal --list-subparsers[=(<baselang>|all)]
#
# - Misc. Opts.:
#     ctags-universal --describe-language=<language>
#     ctags-universal --help-full
#     ctags-universal --quiet[=(yes|no)]
#     ctags-universal --totals[=(yes|no|extra)]
#     ctags-universal -V, --verbose[=(yes|no)]
#
# - REFER:
#   https://docs.ctags.io/en/latest/man/ctags.1.html

# +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++ #

--exclude=.git
--exclude=.svn
--exclude=*.min.js
--exclude=vendors
--exclude=.hg
--exclude=log
--exclude=tmp

# +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++ #

# BACON/2026-05-31: Back on: Disabling this disablement,
# because don't remember why I would've initially disabled,
# perhaps an issue with (old) Exuberant Ctags, maybe file
# size, who knows, other than added for Cyclopath research
# project, circa 2010-2015.
#
#  --languages=-javascript,sql

# REFER: `man ctags-universal` > Extension fields:
#
#   - inherits/i  — When present, value is a comma-separated list of classes
#                   from which this class is derived (i.e. inherits from).
#   - access/a    — Indicates the visibility of this class member, where value
#                   is specific to the language.
#   - signature/S — When present, value is a language-dependent representation
#                   of the signature of a routine....
--fields=+iaS

# REFER: `man ctags-universal` > Extras:
#
#   - inputFile/f — Include an entry for the base file name.
#   - qualified/q — Include an extra class-qualified or namespace-qualified
#       tag entry for each tag which is a member of a class or a namespace.
#       - BECUZ: This may allow easier location of a specific tags [sic] when
#                multiple occurrences of a tag name occur in the tag file.
#       - AWARE: This could potentially more than double the size of the tag file.
--extras=+qf

# Because affects terminal output, let's specify from command invocation.
# - CXREF: infuse_projects_links_core_generate_ctags:
#     ~/.depoxy/ambers/home/.projlns/infuse-projlns-core.sh
#
#  --totals=yes

